# The repo requires Node 24 (`engines.node: "24.x"`; CI and Vercel both build on 24).
#
# WITHOUT this, npm only WARNS on the wrong Node and then fails somewhere else with a
# message that points at the wrong thing. Measured 2026-09-21 on an unmodified lockfile:
#
#   node 24.13.0 / npm 11.6.2  ->  npm ci  exit 0
#   node 22.14.0 / npm 10.9.2  ->  npm ci  EUSAGE "Missing: proxy-agent@8.0.2 from lock file"
#
# The lockfile was correct both times. npm 10 resolves puppeteer's
# `@puppeteer/browsers` peer range differently and demands a nested proxy-agent the
# npm 11 lockfile has no reason to contain — so a TOOLCHAIN mismatch is reported as
# LOCKFILE CORRUPTION. That misdiagnosis cost a real investigation, and nearly cost a
# needless 97-line lockfile rewrite committed as a "fix".
#
# engine-strict makes npm refuse up front with "Unsupported engine", naming the actual
# problem. A wrong-Node install should fail on the wrong Node, not on a lockfile.
engine-strict=true
